[TITLE]
CON-07: two identical 1-acre subcatchments, 50 % impervious, each over its own
copy of aquifer AQ. 0.5 in of rain in the first hour, all of it infiltrates on
the pervious half (f = 5 in/hr). S1's impervious half has 2 in of depression
storage and keeps the 0.5 in ponded until it evaporates; S2's has none.
The pervious halves and aquifers are identical, so groundwater ET must be too.
Evaporation 0.2 in/day, 10 days.

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
INFILTRATION         HORTON
FLOW_ROUTING         KINWAVE
START_DATE           06/01/2020
START_TIME           00:00:00
REPORT_START_DATE    06/01/2020
REPORT_START_TIME    00:00:00
END_DATE             06/11/2020
END_TIME             00:00:00
WET_STEP             00:05:00
DRY_STEP             01:00:00
REPORT_STEP          01:00:00
ROUTING_STEP         0:00:30
IGNORE_ROUTING       YES

[EVAPORATION]
CONSTANT         0.2
DRY_ONLY         NO

[RAINGAGES]
G1   INTENSITY 1:00 1.0 TIMESERIES R1

[SUBCATCHMENTS]
;;Name Gage Outlet Area %Imperv Width %Slope CurbLen
S1   G1   O1   1.0   50   100   1.0   0
S2   G1   O1   1.0   50   100   1.0   0

[SUBAREAS]
;;Name N-Imperv N-Perv S-Imperv S-Perv PctZero RouteTo
S1   0.01   0.1   2.0   0.0   0   OUTLET
S2   0.01   0.1   0.0   0.0   0   OUTLET

[INFILTRATION]
S1   5.0   5.0   4   7   0
S2   5.0   5.0   4   7   0

[AQUIFERS]
;;Name por  WP    FC    Ksat Kslope Tslope ETu  ETs  Seep Ebot Egw Umc
AQ   0.5   0.15   0.30   1.0   10   15   0.35   14   0   0   6   0.30

[GROUNDWATER]
;;Subcatch Aquifer Node Esurf A1 B1 A2 B2 A3 Dsw  (trailing * : see IO-15)
S1   AQ   O1   10   0   0   0   0   0   0   *
S2   AQ   O1   10   0   0   0   0   0   0   *

[OUTFALLS]
O1   0   FREE

[TIMESERIES]
R1   0:00   0.5
R1   1:00   0.0

[REPORT]
SUBCATCHMENTS ALL
